sh value, including literals like `0` and `\"\"`.\n- If that's what you want, disable this lint rule with an inline comment or configure the 'allowObjectTypes' rule option.\n- If you want a type meaning \"any object\", you probably want `object` instead.\n- If you want a type meaning \"any value\", you probably want `unknown` instead.","TSTypeLiteral","noEmptyObject",["1271","1272"],["1273"],"@typescript-eslint/no-unnecessary-type-constraint","Constraining the generic type `T` to `any` does nothing and is unnecessary.","TSTypeParameter","unnecessaryConstraint",["1274"],["1275"],["1276","1277"],["1278"],["1279","1280"],["1281"],"@typescript-eslint/no-wrapper-object-types","Prefer using the primitive `bigint` as a type name, rather than the upper-cased `BigInt`.","bannedClassType",{"range":"1282","text":"1283"},["1284"],"Constraining the generic type `T` to `unknown` does nothing and is unnecessary.",["1285"],["1286"],["1287","1288"],["1289"],"Constraining the generic type `A` to `any` does nothing and is unnecessary.",["1290"],["1291"],["1292","1293"],["1294"],"@typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-function-type","The `Function` type accepts any function-like value.\nPrefer explicitly defining any function parameters and return type.","bannedFunctionType",["1295"],["1296"],["1297"],"Constraining the generic type `A1` to `any` does nothing and is unnecessary.",["1298"],["1299"],["1300","1301"],["1302"],"Constraining the generic type `A2` to `any` does nothing and is unnecessary.",["1303"],["1304"],["1305","1306"],["1307"],["1308","1309"],["1310"],["1311","1312"],["1313"],["1314","1315"],["1316"],["1317","1318"],["1319"],["1320","1321"],["1322"],["1323","1324"],["1325"],["1326","1327"],["1328"],["1329","1330"],["1331"],["1332","1333"],["1334"],["1335","1336"],["1337"],["1338","1339"],["1340"],["1341","1342"],["1343"],["1344","1345"],["1346"],["1347","1348"],["1349"],["1350","1351"],["1352"],["1353","1354"],["1355"],["1356"],["1357"],"'ExtArgs' is defined but never used.",["1358